      "text": "To solve the expression \\(19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2\\), we can use the difference of squares formula, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a-b)(a+b)\\).\n\nLet's break down the expression step by step:\n\n1. \\(19^2 - 17^2 = (19-17)(19+17) = 2 \\cdot 36 = 72\\)\n2. \\(15^2 - 13^2 = (15-13)(15+13) = 2 \\cdot 28 = 56\\)\n3. \\(11^2 - 9^2 = (11-9)(11+9) = 2 \\cdot 20 = 40\\)\n4. \\(9^2 - 7^2 = (9-7)(9+7) = 2 \\cdot 16 = 32\\)\n5. \\(7^2 - 5^2 = (7-5)(7+5) = 2 \\cdot 12 = 24\\)\n6. \\(5^2 - 3^2 = (5-3)(5+3) = 2 \\cdot 8 = 16\\)\n7. \\(3^2 - 1^2 = (3-1)(3+1) = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8\\)\n\nNow, let's substitute these values back into the original expression:\n\n\\[19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2 = 72 + 56 + 40 + 32 + 24 + 16 + 8.\\]\n\nAdding these values together:\n\n\\[72 + 56 = 128\\]\n\\[128 + 40 = 168\\]\n\\[168 + 32 = 200\\]\n\\[200 + 24 = 224\\]\n\\[224 + 16 = 240\\]\n\\[240 + 8 = 248.\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression is \\(\\boxed{248}\\).",
